{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1510466-the-varajtul-mind-virus","id":1510466,"title":"The Varajtul Mind Virus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-01T23:47:50-07:00","id":1510466,"title":"The Varajtul Mind Virus","content":"I will preface this by saying that I know that 2e's treatment of the First Age isn't particularly true anymore. The vibe the new edition is going for is ultimately a different flavor. And I am not dismissing it out of hand. I honestly hope that there is a way to translate some of the (admittedly unpopular) Dreams of the First Age material into 3e, especially using 3d charmsets (which are, admittedly, also a bit unpopular).<br /> <br /> The campaign I am designing in the Second Age is set in the Orchard Isles, especially Rajtul's southern half. I am using it as a stand in mythic Britian, to sort of recreate DnD western european fantasy type settings in an Exalted ruleset and setting in general, with the coasts in the hands of Norse-esque Rajtali sailors (and their Viking raider/pirate bretheren) and a sort of pseudo Albion controlling the southern interior of Rajtul. These vaguely Arthurian knights are a shogunate remnant, a relatively stable Kingdom contrasting to the nearby Satrapies and Faerie Freeholds and whatnot. But, of course, their biggest threat is the Varajtul.<br /> <br /> As I said, I am sort of reluctant to give up the Dreams of the First Age ideas I had enjoyed for the area, including the idea that the Orchard Islands were almost beginner tutorial zones for newly exalted Solars, except the biggest island, which had been shaped by Speaker of Beneficence into his own unique little society with its own language, culture, and cuisine. A little alpine resort, a little northern idealism. <br /> <br /> By the post-apocalyptic Age of Sorrows, this culture became the Varajtul. Named after their fallen capital, and still speaking the old language created for them by the Speaker (as well as the... odd eating habits set down by what became of his lunar husband). Their society had clearly been bent and twisted by the Wyld during the Balorian Crusade.. but.. I cant imagine it was normal during the Shogunate, either.<br /> <br /> In my mind, i remember the old 2e talk of.. embedded mental influences, built into the minds of everyone there. Everyone who spoke the Varajtul language being exposed to.. i guess a mind virus? A society that spread virally. In the first age, it was an artistic expression that shaped generations of mortals into an ideal. The Usurpation reframed it as indoctrination and a dangerous meme, that once heard or read was inescapable. The entire northern half of Rajtul island had to be quarantined to avoid any of their words or ideas to slip out and infect anyone. Extermination didnt work because anyone sent in to do it was changed. Even the Contagion and Crusade didnt stop it, simply warped it by the Wyld into a new iteration.<br /> <br /> But is this possible? Looking through the charms of Solars, can they set something like this up? Ive already decided that Speaker of Beneficence was a Supernal Linguist, but by the time of the Usurpation was already Essence 4 at least, maybe 5. Leaning i to Lore, Socialize, Performance, Presence.. is it possible for that level of Solar to create a mind virus? A culture/society that spreads infectiously, endangering anyone exposed to it? The sort of embedded mental effdcts 2e used to warn that Desus and his ilk were planting into people,necessitating Marama's Fell and other similar situations? If so, what charm combo can do it?<br /> <br /> I mean, i suppose it is all storyteller fiat, and I can handwave it so long as the setting is in the current age of sorrows and not a flashback. But still, I tried to create a beginner level solar version of Speaker of Beneficence, and had NO idea where to go for him to eventually create the Varajtul Mind Virus and a society with embedded ideas that lasted until the Wyld twisted them into something much, much worse. If any of you have found any mind altering combos in 3e, i would love your insight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-02T06:55:39-07:00","id":1510485,"title":"","content":"Honestly I feel like it would work better as a Solar tier Sorcery Working. One of the issue is that if the effect was created by Charms, once the once the Solar Exalt died, the Essence holding those Charm effects would start to dissipate. There aren't many Charms that continue to function for long after the Exalted is dead. Sorcery Workings (or Artifacts or Crafted organisms - perhaps a literal biothaumaturgical virus that infects people) are more permanent and can more easily survive the death of the creator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T07:19:06-07:00","id":1510788,"title":"","content":"I agree that it sounds more like a sorcerous working.<br /> <br /> I think that any writing &quot;necessitating Marama's Fell&quot; needs to be burned out with fire and forgotten. Writers should NOT, ever, write something that &quot;justifies&quot; genocide, period. That kind of writing is utterly abhorrent to me. It should never be part of Exalted, or any game or story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T16:00:09-08:00","id":1525092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1510466-the-varajtul-mind-virus?p=1510788#post1510788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that it sounds more like a sorcerous working.<br /> <br /> I think that any writing &quot;necessitating Marama's Fell&quot; needs to be burned out with fire and forgotten. Writers should NOT, ever, write something that &quot;justifies&quot; genocide, period. That kind of writing is utterly abhorrent to me. It should never be part of Exalted, or any game or story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can relate to the sentiment - in fact it led me to rewrite it as a whole, instead of a death camp (that ethical issues aside, anyone in Creation <i>with basic understanding of occult</i> would know to be a massively boneheaded idea from the get-go), a reservation territory turned social engineering experiment turned cult that then snowballs into religious extremism and mass suicide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}